/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (In the animated film, Sunpebble begins his role excited to represent the university. Over time, he begins noticing contradictions between the image he represents and the realities around him. He sees the equestrian program connected to his own lineage losing institutional support. He notices sustainability messaging that does not always match campus practices. He hears students express uncertainty about what the university actually represents.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
469 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (When Sunpebble raises these concerns privately, he is encouraged to continue smiling and representing the brand without questioning it publicly. Eventually, he decides to leave the university and releases a public statement explaining why. The statement spreads across campus and begins circulating at other universities, prompting conversations about mascots, institutional branding, and how symbols are used to represent identity.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
